sticsearch/issues/comments/1730254173","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/99784#issuecomment-1730254173","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/99784","id":1730254173,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAAe_f85nIZVd","user":{"login":"rjernst","id":289412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTQxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst","html_url":"https://github.com/rjernst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rjernst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-21T20:29:32Z","updated_at":"2023-09-21T20:29:32Z","body":"This is unfortunately how action filters work at the moment. This is not recursive, note that there is a proceed call, followed by the apply of the filter. Proceed is how the chain is traversed. So each of these pair of frames is one instance of an ActionFilter.\r\n\r\nThe root of the problem is the lack of specificity when registering an ActionFilter. All ActionFilters are global, they don't have any notion of applying only to some actions. Thus when the action filters are collected, they are formed into a linear chain that must be searched.\r\n\r\nTBC, we should fix this. But it will require re-engineering how action filters are both registered and invoked.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://a